{"event":"intent","sources":["f001"],"description":"SNAPSHOT=s01; BRANCH=and-presence-guard; Search only snapshots/s01 and no other snapshot for generic-netlink doit handlers whose required-attribute presence guard joins multiple negated presence tests with && instead of || (logical inversion, e.g. 'if (!info->attrs[A] && !info->attrs[B]) return -EINVAL;'), so a message that omits exactly one required attribute passes validation; confirm the absent attributes[] slot is then dereferenced (nla_data/nla_len/nla_get_*/nested parse) yielding a NULL-pointer dereference reachable from unprivileged userspace. For each candidate record function, file:line, and the exact guard plus use; the seed hwsim_del_edge_nl instance itself is never a finding. Save a structured artifact for snapshots/s01 with execution_status, areas searched, candidates, or an evidence-backed negative."}
{"event":"intent","sources":["f001"],"description":"SNAPSHOT=s01; BRANCH=unchecked-tb-deref; Search only snapshots/s01 and no other snapshot for netlink command handlers that dereference an attribute slot (info->attrs[N], tb[N], or nla_data()/nla_get_*() applied to a slot) for which no presence guard and no policy-required/nested-validated entry covers that exact attribute index — including check-one-attribute-then-use-a-different-sibling cases and handlers with no presence check at all; cross-check each candidate against its nla_policy table to prove the slot can be NULL for an attacker-crafted message. Record function, file:line, policy evidence, and reachability. Save a structured artifact for snapshots/s01 with execution_status, areas searched, candidates, or an evidence-backed negative."}
{"event":"intent","sources":["f001"],"description":"SNAPSHOT=s01; BRANCH=nested-parse-null-arg; Search only snapshots/s01 and no other snapshot for nested-attribute parse and iterate helpers — nla_parse_nested, nla_parse_nested_deprecated, nla_validate_nested*, nla_parse_nested_compat, nla_for_each_nested — invoked with the attribute argument taken directly from an optional or unvalidated info->attrs[N]/tb[N] slot so a NULL nesting attribute reaches the helper and is dereferenced inside it; also flag nested parses whose inner attributes are used afterwards without required-flag coverage. Record function, file:line, call-site snippet, and whether the outer attribute is policy-optional. Save a structured artifact for snapshots/s01 with execution_status, areas searched, candidates, or an evidence-backed negative."}
{"event":"intent","sources":["f001"],"description":"SNAPSHOT=s01; BRANCH=rtnl-doit-attr-gaps; Search only snapshots/s01 and no other snapshot for rtnetlink RTM_* doit/setlink/newlink/dellink/getlink/changelink/dumpit handlers (rtnl_register, rtnl_link_ops, per-kind policies) where nlmsg_parse/nlmsg_find_attr or parsed tb[] results are indexed and dereferenced without a per-attribute NULL check covering that exact attribute — including kind-specific setlink/changelink paths reading IFLA_*/driver attributes after only partial validation, and paths feeding optional attributes into lengths or indices. Record function, file:line, the missing check, and reachability. Save a structured artifact for snapshots/s01 with execution_status, areas searched, candidates, or an evidence-backed negative."}
